  chef: {fileID: 11400000, guid: d4ca161307a19ab499b5d49387c6380d, type: 2}
  letterBody: 'Hey again!


    Dan here. Heard your place is getting real busy.
    Proud of you, kid, and I don''t even know you.


    This pie is my late wife''s.
    Mary baked it every Sunday for the diner, and folks drove an hour just for a
    slice. After she passed, I couldn''t make it for two years. Then one day a regular
    asked for "Mary''s pie," and I figured she''d want it served, not missed.


    Cold
    butter in the crust, apples with sugar and cinnamon, bake till the juice bubbles.


    Some
    recipes are meant to keep going.'
